{"title":"The Hell Mouth","link":"https://kottke.org/26/07/the-hell-mouth","date":1785430320000,"content":"\n         \t<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//plus/misc/images/editor-1785359827-78f7c764.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none//plus/misc/images/editor-1785359827-78f7c764.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//plus/misc/images/editor-1785359827-78f7c764.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n\t<p>Volcanologist Laszlo Kestay took <a href=\"https://www.usgs.gov/media/images/west-kamokuna-skylight\">this photo</a> of a <a href=\"https://www.usgs.gov/news/truth-about-terrifying-lava-skylight-where-only-trained-should-lurk\">lava skylight</a> in 1996 while conducting field work at Kīlauea on Hawaiʻi. The hardened lava flows strongly resemble doomed souls being sucked into hell or the damned escaping the underworld.\n</p>\n \n\n        \n         <p><strong>Tags:</strong> <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/geology\">geology</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/hawaii\">hawaii</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/hell\">hell</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/Laszlo%20Kestay\">Laszlo Kestay</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/photography\">photography</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/volcanoes\">volcanoes</a></p>\n        \n    ","author":"Jason Kottke","siteTitle":"Kottke","siteHash":"89a883271b4598f9b33ebe87be70d38557bcd266e68aee521a8f93622e0ab723","entryHash":"20c9ebad7491f3fc25318f4138d7c56944adc580106861b74481125d88615404","category":"Sites"}